                  <provenance type="#i"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_404">Norwich, Norfolk.
                        Benedictine cathedral priory of Holy Trinity</orgName><p>"Liber ffratris
                        Willelmi Spynk monachi Norwic'".</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Part of lot 449 in the Sherbrooke sale at
                     Sotheby's 27 June 1912. The lot was purchased by Barnard, and sold to the
                     Rylands who split it up as i) R.32528, ii) R.32548, iii) MS. Lat. 226, q. v.
                     Norwich, iv) MS. Lat. 185, 8 leaves s. xiv.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">The old binding appears to have been
                     contemporary, the items coming in the order iii, i, ii, iv. iii &amp; iv were
                     no doubt binding pads.</provenance>
               </history>
